<title>BELGIUM: EU's de Silguy says EMU delay impossible.</title>
<headline>EU's de Silguy says EMU delay impossible.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A postponement to Europe's planned single currency is legally and practically impossible, EU monetary affairs commissioner Yves Thibault de Silguy said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Speaking to a committee at the European Parliament, de Silguy said: &quot;In practical terms and legal terms there is no way we can postpone.&quot;</p>
<p>He added that a delay to the 1999 timetable would prompt legal action from large banks and businesses which have invested billions in preparing for monetary union.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 32 2 287 6838</p>
